  "description": "The KellyKapowski run is configured to operate in three dimensions using a gradient step of 0.025 and a total of four processing threads. Tissue labeling follows the standard convention with the white\u2011matter label set to 3 and the gray\u2011matter label set to 2. The algorithm employs a smoothing velocity field of 1.5 and a smoothing variance of 1, while the maximum number of iterations for inverting the displacement field is limited to 20. Integration is performed with ten points per segment, and the thickness prior is estimated at 10\u202fmm. Additional command\u2011line arguments include \u201c--verbose\u201d, and convergence is targeted at a tolerance of 0.001. B\u2011spline smoothing is enabled for the final surface refinement.\n\nAll required inputs are supplied: the segmentation image, the white\u2011matter probability map, the gray\u2011matter probability map, the cortical thickness map, the warped white\u2011matter image, and the thickness prior image. These data will be processed together under the settings described above."
